# Recipe: file sharing

Use app-owned Hyperdrive operations for file storage and
`@unstoppable-stack/p2p/sync` for resource mirroring. Read `modules/p2p.mdc`,
the `add-file-storage` skill and installed P2P `docs/sync.md`.

Attach `syncPack({ store })` to the existing node on the source and replica
host. Pair with explicit grants. Send the replica's `sync` capability a complete
`manifest.replace` request with `schemaVersion: 1` and resources containing
id, kind `hyperdrive`, actual core key, name and protection mode `mirror`.
Inspect peer-scoped status before claiming a local checkpoint is available.

Do not create another swarm/store around the sync pack. Apps own drive reads,
writes, large-file streams and any filesystem import/export. `/sync` is not a
file download/range RPC or selective path ACL API. Keep private files separate;
key sharing permits replication and revocation does not erase downloaded copies.
Replicate before reads. Test transfer and source-offline replica restart;
mirroring is not complete backup acceptance.
